# Authoring a wiki page

When creating or editing a file under `wiki/pages/`, keep it lint-clean
(`llmwiki lint --strict`).

## Required frontmatter
- `id` — canonical, opaque, unique (e.g. `entity:open-knowledge-format`). Never
  change it on rename; add old names to `aliases` instead.
- `title`, `slug`, `type` (`entity|topic|note|index`), `status`
  (`candidate|reviewed|disputed|stale|superseded|retracted`).

## Grounding
- Reviewed `entity`/`topic` pages must carry `sources` and `claims`.
- Each claim needs `text` and, when `reviewed`/`disputed`, `evidence` with a
  `source_id` that exists in the page's `sources` list, plus a `locator`.
- Record each source's `uri`, a `sha256:` `digest`, and `rights`.

## Links & freshness
- Use `[[Wikilinks]]`; every target must resolve to an existing page.
- Set `freshness.checked_at`; if `expires_at` passes, the linter flags it stale.
- If `rights.redistribution_allowed: true`, declare a `license_expression`.

## Discipline
- Prefer editing an existing page over creating a duplicate identity.
- Contradictions are kept, not overwritten — set `status: disputed`.
- Deletions are tombstones — set `status: retracted`, don't erase history.
